      trivia: "The origin of the Corojo leaf trails a tale of smuggling. In the 1960s a very small quantity of Authentic Corojo seed taken out of Cuba found its way to the Jamastran Valley, and the Eiroa family, perfecting its cultivation over forty years, is said to have become one of the world's few custodians of “genuine Corojo”. The valley is held to share an almost identical microclimate with Cuba's Vuelta Abajo, its distinct wet and dry seasons conferring a singular flavour. The work of Dylan Austin, who led the great overhaul of 2013, has been rated among the most successful rebrandings in the history of the premium cigar."
