      trivia: "The company name “CLE” is nothing other than the initials of founder Christian Luis Eiroa. The “Cuarenta” (Spanish for forty), one of the launch cigars of 2012, marks the fortieth birthday Eiroa reached that July. The commemorative Eiroa “The First 20 Years” was fashioned from ten-year-aged Corojo presented by his father Julio for his twentieth year in the industry (2015), its binder said to have been heirloom-grade leaf unused for more than fifty years. It is the story of the “Corojo King” who raised Camacho into a world-class marque, staking his own name on independence."
